WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.820 align:start position:0%
 
[Applause]  [Music]  [Applause]  russia warned that it would attack the  nato resupply routes and that is what  they did  a barrage of missiles struck the  military base just before 4 am on sunday  morning  this base has been a hub for some of the  weapons that have been brought in from  europe and a center to train foreign  fighters joining the conflict  we don't know if any of them were killed  driving towards the scene we passed  ambulance after ambulance coming the  other way  rushing the wound into hospital  it seemed quite likely to us that the  death toll would be far higher than  first reported  as we reached a village close to the  base the air raid sirens sounded again  [Music]  sending people running for the shelters  after the strikes overnight they were  visibly frightened the russians were  coming for them again  the wounded were taken to a nearby  hospital  we watched as more and more arrive  throughout the morning some with serious  injuries to their heads and limbs  by lunchtime the hospital was full  ambulances queued outside to take the  wounded elsewhere  this soldier told me that the first  missile struck before the warning signs  had even gone off it was like hell he  said  many of the wounded asked us not to film  their faces their families have fled to  europe whilst they've stayed behind to  help and they understandably don't want  them to see what's happened  it is too early to know whether this is  a new front in the war  or just a one-off attack  either way no one here or in nato's  capitals will sleep easy tonight  aleister bunkel sky news in western  ukraine

